# sys-follower-talk: follower talk (OpenSinnoh option `followerTalk` with the HGSS add-on; run by
# tests/integration/follower-talk.rom.test.ts with both ROMs). Route 202 with Turtwig as the lead: two steps north,
# the follower comes out behind; the player turns to it (it stands in front, in view) and presses A. It turns to the player, HGSS's rules pick an
# interaction, and its messages close with A. Talked to twice; the field is idle (and saveable) only afterwards.
party 0 platinum:SPECIES_TURTWIG 20
set state repel 250
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_ROUTE_202 171 809 up
until idle
+0 press up
until position 171 807
+0 release up
until idle
+0 assert state partyFollower.z 808
# talk
+1 press down
+1 release down
until idle
+0 assert facing player down
+1 press a
+1 release a
until message 300
advance text 600
until idle 300
+0 assert state partyFollower.facing "up"
+1 press a
+1 release a
until message 300
advance text 600
until idle 300
+0 assert position platinum:MAP_HEADER_ROUTE_202 171 807
